  "what_the_study_did": "The study explored how to strategically combine toxicological tests to maximize their predictive power, using the prediction of cardiac arrhythmia torsade de pointes as an example.",
  "what_it_found": "Tests can be strategically combined to reach a desired level of predictive power, which is generally more easily achieved for negative predictive power when the toxicity prevalence is low.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Overall, the analysis demonstrates that tests can be strategically combined to reach a desired level of predictive power.",
      "topic": "Strategic Test Combination"
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is generally more easily achieved for negative predictive power given a low prevalence of the toxicity under scrutiny.",
      "topic": "Negative Predictive Power"
    },
    {
      "quote": "For this work, we used a base prevalence of 10% for a substance to carry a tordsadogenic liability.",
      "topic": "Base Prevalence"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Given uncertainty around a test's discriminatory power, a probabilistic rather than deterministic approach was recommended.",
      "topic": "Probabilistic Approach"
    },
    {
      "quote": "The proposed approach is easily implemented deterministically since values of the discriminatory power of the tests are readily and publicly available.",
      "topic": "Deterministic Implementation"
    },
    {
      "quote": "This general approach could form a basis for testing and decision-making that can be communicated and discussed in a consistent manner between scientists as well as between sponsors and regulators.",
      "topic": "Communication Basis"
    }
  ]
}
